  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nAs water continues down the Mon/Musk rivers and their \ntributaries, it may raise some sites near-to-above action \nthrough eastern Ohio and along the Mon/Ohio rivers. Otherwise, \ndry weather and limited precipitation chances are forecast over \nthe next 7 days as the region remains in dry, northwest flow \nbetween a central CONUS ridge and a 500mb low over the Canadian \nMaritimes. \n\nTemperatures will remain stable, with the 25th to 75th\npercentiles for highs and lows each day in the 70s and 50s\nrespectively. A series of shortwave lows will swing around the\nclosed 500mb low early-to-mid week, providing low chances of\nrain. Timing will mostly be tied to exact shortwave timing, \nwhich remains uncertain, though PoPs remain slight chance at \nbest. No hazardous weather expected.",
